  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Essential hypertension, stage 1, on lifestyle measures (I10)</content>. Home average down from 138/88 to 136/86 mmHg, still above the target below 130/80. Urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio 8 mg/g, normal, so no kidney damage. Lifestyle measures continue as planned. [S]<list><item>Continue lifestyle measures.</item><item>Home readings before the three-month visit, where medicine will be decided.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Nicotine dependence, pipe tobacco (F17.290)</content>. Abstinent for five weeks. [S]<list><item>Continue varenicline.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Pre-expedition dental, hearing and vision checks</content>. Dental examination: no caries or gum disease; teeth cleaned; no further treatment needed before departure. Audiometry today: hearing thresholds 20 dB or better at all frequencies in both ears. Eye examination: distance vision 6/6 in each eye; early presbyopia; reading glasses prescribed. [S]<list><item>Carry a spare pair of reading glasses and glacier glasses with side shields.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Office blood pressure, validated technique, average of two readings (target below 130/80 mmHg)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>136/86 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Home blood pressure monitoring to confirm the diagnosis and guide treatment</td><td>At diagnosis and when treatment changes</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Seven-day average 136/86 mmHg on lifestyle measures</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight, BMI, and cardiac auscultation</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>71.6 kg, BMI 23.9; no murmur</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio</td><td>At diagnosis, then yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>8 mg/g, normal. Protocol deviation: the test was due at diagnosis and was collected about four weeks late, because no urine was given at intake and the gap was not caught then. No harm resulted: the result is normal and did not change the plan. Corrective action: collect the urine sample at the visit when hypertension is suspected</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Basic metabolic panel: sodium, potassium, creatinine, eGFR</td><td>Baseline; 2 to 4 weeks after starting an ARB; then every 6 months on an ARB</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Baseline normal at intake; not on an ARB</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Echocardiogram</td><td>Only for stage 2 hypertension, suspected left ventricular hypertrophy, or clinical change</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Stage 1; no left ventricular hypertrophy</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Fundoscopic examination</td><td>Yearly</td><td>Due</td><td>At the preventive visit in two weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Tobacco use and cessation support (varenicline with counseling)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Abstinent for five weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Pre-expedition dental, hearing, and vision checks</td><td>Once before departure</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Dental examination and cleaning, audiometry, and eye examination complete; all normal apart from early presbyopia</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Frostbite and hypothermia prevention and field treatment training</td><td>Before departure</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Course booked for next month</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Home blood pressure average below 130/80 mmHg before departure. In progress; target 1910-05-26 [S]</item><item>No tobacco from the quit date, confirmed at each visit. In progress; target 1910-05-26 [S]</item><item>Complete a wilderness first aid course with frostbite, hypothermia and evacuation practice before departure. In progress; target 1910-04-21 [S]</item><item>A written expedition medical plan covering nutrition and vitamin C, cold injury, altitude, mental health support, medicines and evacuation, agreed before departure. In progress; target 1910-05-26 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: 2025 AHA/ACC/AANP/AAPA/ABC/ACCP/ACPM/AGS/AMA/ASPC/NMA/PCNA/SGIM Guideline for the Prevention, Detection, Evaluation and Management of High Blood Pressure in Adults (Jones DW, et al. Circulation 2025;152(11):e114-e218) (2025); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, hypertension monograph (2026); Tobacco Smoking Cessation in Adults, Including Pregnant Persons: Interventions (2021); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Preventive visit in two weeks. Three-month review in eight weeks with home readings. Next scheduled visit 1910-03-10: periodic adult preventive visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
